<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: right; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <span data-field="initials">{{ initials }}</span><br>
    <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span>
  </div>
  <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 10px;">Academic Achievement Programs (AAP) Computer Laptop Lending Program</h1>
  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; text-align: center; margin-top: 0;">Borrower Responsibilities and Guidelines</h2>

  <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Purpose</h3>
  <p style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5;">The purpose of the AAP Computer Laptop Lending Program is to provide a mobile computer resource to those AAP students who may not own a PC and/or laptop computer and are in need of computer resources for University related projects.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5;">The laptops provided through this program are configured to the University's wireless network and include the following software: Windows Vista Home Basic version, Windows XP Professional Version with SP2, Office 2007 Professional/Office 2003 Professional, McAfee Antivirus, and MSN Live Messenger.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5;">Laptop computers for all eligible <span data-field="student_type">{{ student_type }}</span> students must be checked out from the IT staff in <span data-field="location">{{ location }}</span> hours during which laptop computers can be checked out are limited to the following:</p>

  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 50%; padding: 5px 0;">Monday</td>
      <td style="width: 50%; padding: 5px 0;">10 a.m.-2 p.m.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 50%; padding: 5px 0;">Thursday</td>
      <td style="width: 50%; padding: 5px 0;">10 a.m.-2 p.m.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Borrower Responsibilities and Guidelines</h3>
  <ol style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6;">
    <li>Each Borrower must complete an AAP Checkout and Liability form in which s/he acknowledges responsibility for the laptop computer and peripherals checked out under his/her name.</li>
    <li>The AAP laptop lending program is only open to borrowers who do not own their own laptops.</li>
    <li>The AAP laptop lending program operates on a first come, first served basis.</li>
    <li>The Borrower is financially responsible for:
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
        <li>Full replacement cost of the laptop computer and all peripherals checked out under his/her name if lost or stolen during the checkout period.</li>
        <li>Full repair costs if the computer or any peripherals are damaged in any way, including spills from food or drink.</li>
        <li>Damage or loss charges will be applied directly to the Borrower's University account.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Laptop Checkout options are as follows:
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
        <li>3 day checkout</li>
        <li>1 week checkout</li>
      </ul>
      If there is no student waiting list, when the laptop is returned, the Borrower may renew the checkout for a maximum of 1 week. Borrowers who do not adhere to this return policy will forfeit their eligibility to participate in the AAP computer lending program.
    </li>
    <li>If a computer and/or peripherals are not returned, this will be considered theft of University property and appropriate actions will be taken.</li>
    <li>Neither the University nor AAP is responsible for any computer viruses that may be transferred to, or from, a user's disk or network account.</li>
    <li>Personal software may not be loaded onto the laptop at any time.</li>
    <li>All files created while using the AAP laptop must be saved to floppy disk, CD or DVD. No files should be saved to the laptop's hard drive.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: right; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <span data-field="initials">{{ initials }}</span><br>
    <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span>
  </div>
  <ol style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6;">
    <li>Violation of the policies listed above will be grounds for refusal of service in the future and/or fines.</li>
    <li>All use of the AAP laptops must comply with the University's Guidelines for Acceptable Use of Computing Resources, which can be viewed at <a href="http://www.netethics.umd.edu/aup/index.html" style="color: blue;">{{ university_guidelines_url }}</a>.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

